<!--
    Objective-C declarations typed by class (`option objc on|off`,
    `option objcivars on|off`).

    Issue: a method's own type encoding spells every object as a bare `@`, so
    with the instance structs of `objcivars` in place only `self` was typed:
    a getter returned `objc_object *`, its setter took one, an ivar of a class
    of this image was an `objc_object *` and a field read through any of them
    stayed `*(int *)((long)v + 8)`. The class is in the metadata: a property's
    attribute string (`T@"Base",&,N,Vinner`) and an ivar's encoding (`@"Base"`)
    name it.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement. `analyzers/objc/kuna_objcprops.rs`
    reads the `property_list_t` of every class, metaclass, category and
    protocol into getter/setter encodings that name the class;
    `Selectors::record` keeps the class-naming spelling of two agreeing
    declarations; the encoding decoder resolves `@"Base"` to the struct the
    `objcivars` layout built (a record declared before its layout lands reads
    the completion), so the typed pointer reaches P5 field resolution.

    P0 assertions: `option objc on|off`, `option objcivars on|off`.

    The fixture is `macho_objc_types.m`: `Base { isa; int count }` with a
    synthesized `count` property, `Holder : Base { Base *inner }` with a
    synthesized `inner` property, and `-[Holder innerCount]` reading
    `inner->count`, `[inner count]` and `[[self inner] count]` (the last through
    an `objc_msgSend$inner` stub).

    Pass 1 (`objc off`) reproduces the BUG: `sub_100000740(void *a0)` reads
    `*(int4 *)(((int8 *)a0)[2] + 8)`.
    Pass 2 (`objc on`, `objcivars off`) shows the declarations alone: the getter
    is `Base * -[Holder inner](objc_object *self, ...)` and the stub result is a
    `Base *v3`, but with no layout for `self` the read is still through casts.
    Pass 3 (`objc on`) is the FIX: `v1 = self->inner->count;`, the getter returns
    `self->inner` as `Base *`, and `-[Holder setInner:]` takes `Base *arg1`.
-->
